                <pb facs="0360" n="348" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg348"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 E.W./10–1545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Representative in Bulgaria</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Barnes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-15T18:00:00+02:00">October 15, 1945—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 15—2:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>604. General Crane states Greek claims signed by Greek Foreign Minister as
                    demanded by Biryusov have now been presented by Greek liaison mission and that
                    mission’s financial requirements have been set through action Bulgarian Foreign
                    Ministry; therefore he and General Oxley do not think communication to ACC in
                    sense of Department’s 329, October 10, desirable at this time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Barnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
